    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** serving as the undisputed anchor of the lineup. With a massive 85.10 efficiency score, **Corbin Carroll** is our primary offensive engine against Buehler, benefiting from a favorable 4.46 xERA matchup and an 8% boost from the second spot in the order. He is flanked by **Max Muncy** (68.90) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (68.19), both of whom capitalize on a soft matchup against Abbott, whose 5.06 xERA provides the high-ceiling environment we need to chase counting stats. While **Henry Bolte** (65.39) and **Gabriel Moreno** (66.21) offer strong supporting value, the platoon edge against the vulnerable Abbott makes stacking against him a priority for our daily production.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved the benching of **Zach McKinstry**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 33.54 score. While he typically adds depth, the combination of a tough matchup against Miller (3.39 xERA) and a drop to the #9 spot in the order cratered his efficiency below our 40-point \"Zebras\" floor. We remain cautious with **Brice Turang** (50.39); while his leadoff status provides volume, his matchup against Ashcraft is neutralized by an elite catcher pop-time disadvantage, making him a marginal play compared to the higher-upside profiles like **Seiya Suzuki** (47.88), who faces the toughest arm of the day in Cease. We are closely monitoring the status of **Josh Naylor**, **James Wood**, and **Vinnie Pasquantino** as they recover from their respective IL stints; their absence continues to constrain our utility options and forces us to rely on the depth of **Travis Bazzana** and **Cole Young** to maintain our sprint speed metrics and category viability in a tight Roto race.",
